PKG-CONFIG(1)             BSD General Commands Manual            PKG-CONFIG(1)

NNAAMMEE
     ppkkgg--ccoonnffiigg — a system for configuring build dependency information

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppkkgg--ccoonnffiigg [_o_p_t_i_o_n_s] _m_o_d_u_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppkkgg--ccoonnffiigg program retrieves configuration information related to the
     _m_o_d_u_l_e arguments from pc(5) files installed on the system and prints
     parts of the retrieved information depending on the specified _o_p_t_i_o_n_s.
     The most common use is printing the compiler and linker flags needed to
     build software that uses the libraries given by the _m_o_d_u_l_e arguments.

     The pc(5) files are searched for along a path constructed from the
     ----wwiitthh--ppaatthh option, the PKG_CONFIG_PATH and PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR environment
     variables, and some compiled-in default directories.  The _m_o_d_u_l_e argu‐
     ments correspond to the file names, but without the _._p_c filename exten‐
     sion.

     Several of the _o_p_t_i_o_n_s cause immediate exit.  If multiple of these op‐
     tions are given, only the option with the highest priority takes effect
     and those with lower priority are silently ignored.  These options are,
     ordered by descending priority:

     1.   No-module options: ----rreellooccaattee, ----dduummpp--ppeerrssoonnaalliittyy, ----aabboouutt,
          ----vveerrssiioonn, ----hheellpp, ----aattlleeaasstt--ppkkggccoonnffiigg--vveerrssiioonn, ----lliisstt--aallll, and
          ----lliisstt--ppaacckkaaggee--nnaammeess: These options cause all arguments to be ig‐
          nored.

     2.   Argument-only options: ----aattlleeaasstt--vveerrssiioonn, ----eexxaacctt--vveerrssiioonn, and
          ----mmaaxx--vveerrssiioonn: These options only inspect modules explicitly speci‐
          fied on the command line and do not look at dependencies.

     3.   Limited-output options: ----vvaalliiddaattee, ----lliicceennssee, ----uunniinnssttaalllleedd, and
          ----eennvv: These options perform dependency resolution, but exit after
          printing the information requested by the highest-priority option,
          ignoring other output options that may have been specified.

     Several other options require at least one _m_o_d_u_l_e argument, produce out‐
     put, do not cause early exit, can be combined with each other, but over‐
     ride and disable all ----ccffllaaggss and ----lliibbss options:

     1.   Single-module output options: ----ppaatthh, ----pprriinntt--vvaarriiaabblleess, ----vvaarriiaabbllee:
          If any of these options is specified, only the first _m_o_d_u_l_e argument
          is used, all other arguments are silently ignored, and no dependency
          resolution is attempted.

     2.   Depth-one output options: ----pprriinntt--pprroovviiddeess, ----mmooddvveerrssiioonn,
          ----pprriinntt--rreeqquuiirreess, and ----pprriinntt--rreeqquuiirreess--pprriivvaattee: If any of these op‐
          tions is specified, only modules explicitly specified on the command
          line are inspected and no dependency resolution is attempted.

     3.   General output options: ----ssiimmuullaattee, ----ddiiggrraapphh, ----ssoolluuttiioonn,
          ----ffrraaggmmeenntt--ttrreeee: These options do not limit dependency resolution.

     The most important output options ----ccffllaaggss and ----lliibbss can be combined
     with each other, but are overridden and ignored if any of the options
     listed above are specified.

     The complete list of _o_p_t_i_o_n_s is as follows:

     ----aabboouutt
             Print the version number, the Copyright notice, and the license
             of the ppkkgg--ccoonnffiigg program to standard output and exit.  Most
             other options and all command line arguments are ignored.

     ----aattlleeaasstt--ppkkggccoonnffiigg--vveerrssiioonn=_v_e_r_s_i_o_n
             Exit with error if the requested _v_e_r_s_i_o_n number is greater than
             the version number of the ppkkgg--ccoonnffiigg program, or with success
             otherwise.  Most other options and all command line arguments are
             ignored.

     ----aattlleeaasstt--vveerrssiioonn=_v_e_r_s_i_o_n
             Check the _m_o_d_u_l_e arguments in the given order.  Exit with error
             as soon as a _m_o_d_u_l_e does not exist, and exit with success as soon
             as the version number of a _m_o_d_u_l_e is greater than or equal to the
             requested _v_e_r_s_i_o_n number.  Exit with error if the version number
             of each _m_o_d_u_l_e is less than the requested _v_e_r_s_i_o_n number.

     ----ccffllaaggss, ----ccffllaaggss--oonnllyy--II, ----ccffllaaggss--oonnllyy--ootthheerr
             Print all compiler flags required to compile against the _m_o_d_u_l_e,
             or only the include path (--II) flags, or only the compiler flags
             that are not include path flags, respectively.  These options im‐
             ply ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss.

     ----ddeebbuugg
             Print some non-fatal warning messages to standard error output
             that would otherwise silently be ignored.  This option also im‐
             plies ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss.  If ppkkgg--ccoonnffiigg was compiled without defin‐
             ing the preprocessor macro PKGCONF_LITE, this option also prints
             many debugging messages to standard error output.

     ----ddeeffiinnee--pprreeffiixx
             Attempts to determine the prefix variable to use for CFLAGS and
             LIBS entry relocations.  This is mainly useful for platforms
             where framework SDKs are relocatable, such as Windows.

     ----ddeeffiinnee--vvaarriiaabbllee=_v_a_r_n_a_m_e=_v_a_l_u_e
             Define _v_a_r_n_a_m_e as _v_a_l_u_e.  Variables are used in query output, and
             some modules' results may change based on the presence of a vari‐
             able definition.

     ----ddiiggrraapphh
             Dump the dependency resolver's solution as a graphviz ‘dot’ file.
             This can be used with graphviz to visualize module interdependen‐
             cies.  This option is only available if the preprocessor macro
             PKGCONF_LITE was not defined during compilation.

     ----ddoonntt--ddeeffiinnee--pprreeffiixx
             Disables the ‘define-prefix’ feature.

     ----ddoonntt--rreellooccaattee--ppaatthhss
             Disables the path relocation feature.

     ----dduummpp--ppeerrssoonnaalliittyy
             Print some default settings to standard output, in particular the
             default module search path that is used when PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR is
             not defined, the default list of include paths that are filtered
             out when PKG_CONFIG_SYSTEM_INCLUDE_PATH is not defined, and the
             default list of library paths that are filtered out when
             PKG_CONFIG_SYSTEM_LIBRARY_PATH is not defined, and exit.  Most
             other options and all command line arguments are ignored.  This
             option is only available if the preprocessor macro PKGCONF_LITE
             was not defined during compilation.

     ----eennvv=_v_a_r_n_a_m_e
             Print the requested values as variable declarations in a similar
             format as the env(1) command.

     ----eennvv--oonnllyy
             Initialize the module search path from ----wwiitthh--ppaatthh and
             PKG_CONFIG_PATH only, ignoring PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR and the com‐
             piled-in default directories.

     ----eerrrroorrss--ttoo--ssttddoouutt
             Print all error, warning, and debugging messages to standard out‐
             put instead of to standard error output.

     ----eexxaacctt--vveerrssiioonn=_v_e_r_s_i_o_n
             Check the _m_o_d_u_l_e arguments in the given order.  Exit with error
             as soon as a _m_o_d_u_l_e does not exist, and exit with success as soon
             as the version number of a _m_o_d_u_l_e is exactly the requested
             _v_e_r_s_i_o_n number.  Exit with error if the version number of each
             _m_o_d_u_l_e differs from the requested _v_e_r_s_i_o_n number.

     ----eexxiissttss
             Exit with a non-zero exit status if the dependency resolver is
             unable to find all of the requested _m_o_d_u_l_es.  This option is ac‐
             tive by default and cannot be disabled.  However, various other
             options cause ppkkgg--ccoonnffiigg to exit and report success or failure
             before all arguments have been inspected.

     ----ffrraaggmmeenntt--ffiilltteerr=_t_y_p_e_s
             Filter the fragment lists for the specified _t_y_p_e_s.

     ----hheellpp  Print a usage summary on standard output and exit.  Most other
             options and all command line arguments are ignored.

     ----iiggnnoorree--ccoonnfflliiccttss
             Ignore ‘Conflicts’ rules in modules.

     ----kkeeeepp--ssyysstteemm--ccffllaaggss, ----kkeeeepp--ssyysstteemm--lliibbss
             Keep CFLAGS or linker flag fragments that would be filtered due
             to being included by default in the compiler.

     ----lliibbss, ----lliibbss--oonnllyy--LL, ----lliibbss--oonnllyy--ll, ----lliibbss--oonnllyy--ootthheerr
             Print all linker flags required to link against the _m_o_d_u_l_e, or
             only the library path (--LL) flags, or only the library (--ll) flags,
             or only the linker flags that are neither library path nor li‐
             brary flags, respectively.  These options imply ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss.

     ----lliisstt--aallll
             Walk the module search path in the order of descending priority.
             For each pc(5) file found, print one line to standard output,
             containing the basename of the file without the extension, the
             NNaammee property, a dash (‘-’), and the DDeessccrriippttiioonn property.  This
             option implies ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss.  All command line arguments are
             ignored.

     ----lliisstt--ppaacckkaaggee--nnaammeess
             Perform the same search as ----lliisstt--aallll, but only print the base‐
             name of each pc(5) file without the extension, not the module
             name and the description.  This option implies ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss.
             All command line arguments are ignored.

     ----lloogg--ffiillee=_f_i_l_e
             Set the name of the output _f_i_l_e where information about selected
             modules is logged, both about those selected by arguments and as
             dependencies.  For each selected module, one line is printed,
             containing the basename of the pc(5) file without the extension,
             optionally an operator and version number describing the desired
             range of versions, and either the actual version number in square
             brackets or the string "NOT-FOUND".  If this option is not pro‐
             vided, the name of the output file is instead taken from the
             PKG_CONFIG_LOG environment variable, and if that is not provided
             either, this kind of logging is disabled.

     ----mmaaxx--vveerrssiioonn=_v_e_r_s_i_o_n
             Check the _m_o_d_u_l_e arguments in the given order.  Exit with error
             as soon as a _m_o_d_u_l_e does not exist, and exit with success as soon
             as the version number of a _m_o_d_u_l_e is less than or equal to the
             requested _v_e_r_s_i_o_n number.  Exit with error if the version number
             of each _m_o_d_u_l_e is greater than the requested _v_e_r_s_i_o_n number.

     ----mmaaxxiimmuumm--ttrraavveerrssee--ddeepptthh=_d_e_p_t_h
             Impose a limit on the allowed depth in the dependency graph.  For
             example, a _d_e_p_t_h of 2 restricts the resolver from acting on child
             dependencies of modules added to the resolver's solution.  This
             option is overridden by the PKG_CONFIG_MAXIMUM_TRAVERSE_DEPTH en‐
             vironment variable and by the options ----mmooddvveerrssiioonn, ----ppaatthh,
             ----pprriinntt--pprroovviiddeess, ----pprriinntt--rreeqquuiirreess, ----pprriinntt--rreeqquuiirreess--pprriivvaattee,
             ----pprriinntt--vvaarriiaabblleess, and ----vvaarriiaabbllee.

     ----mmooddvveerrssiioonn
             For each specified _m_o_d_u_l_e, print the version number to standard
             output.  If the ----vveerrbboossee option is also specified, the name of
             the respective _m_o_d_u_l_e and a colon is printed before each version
             number.  This option implies ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss and
             ----mmaaxxiimmuumm--ttrraavveerrssee--ddeepptthh=1 and overrides and disables all
             ----ccffllaaggss and ----lliibbss flags.

     ----mmssvvcc--ssyynnttaaxx
             Use MSVC syntax for ----ccffllaaggss, ----eennvv, and ----lliibbss output.  This op‐
             tion is only available if the preprocessor macro PKGCONF_LITE was
             not defined during compilation.

     ----nnoo--ccaacchhee
             Skip caching packages when they are loaded into the internal re‐
             solver.  This may result in an alternate dependency graph being
             computed.

     ----nnoo--pprroovviiddeess
             Ignore ‘Provides’ rules in modules when resolving dependencies.

     ----nnoo--uunniinnssttaalllleedd
             Forbids the dependency resolver from considering 'uninstalled'
