     ----pprreeffiixx--vvaarriiaabbllee=_v_a_r_i_a_b_l_e
             Sets the ‘prefix’ variable used by the ‘define-prefix’ feature.

     ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss
             Print some messages about fatal errors to standard error output
             that would otherwise be omitted.  This option is implied by many
             other options, but not by all.  It can be overridden with
             ----ssiilleennccee--eerrrroorrss.

     ----pprriinntt--pprroovviiddeess
             For each specified _m_o_d_u_l_e, print one line to standard output con‐
             taining the NNaammee property, an equal sign (‘=’), and the VVeerrssiioonn
             property.  If the _m_o_d_u_l_e contains one or more PPrroovviiddeess proper‐
             ties, print additional lines in dependency list format, one name
             per line, each name optionally followed by an operator and a ver‐
             sion.  This option implies ----mmaaxxiimmuumm--ttrraavveerrssee--ddeepptthh=1 and over‐
             rides and disables all ----ccffllaaggss and ----lliibbss flags.

     ----pprriinntt--rreeqquuiirreess, ----pprriinntt--rreeqquuiirreess--pprriivvaattee
             For each specified _m_o_d_u_l_e, print the RReeqquuiirreess or RReeqquuiirreess..pprriivvaattee
             properties, respectively, in dependency list format to standard
             output.  Both of these options imply ----mmaaxxiimmuumm--ttrraavveerrssee--ddeepptthh=1
             and override and disable all ----ccffllaaggss and ----lliibbss flags.

     ----pprriinntt--vvaarriiaabblleess
             For the first _m_o_d_u_l_e given on the command line, print the names
             of all seen variables to standard output, one per line.  Any sub‐
             sequent arguments are silently ignored.  This option implies
             ----pprriinntt--eerrrroorrss and ----mmaaxxiimmuumm--ttrraavveerrssee--ddeepptthh=1 and overrides and
             disables all ----ccffllaaggss and ----lliibbss flags.

     ----ppuurree  Treats the computed dependency graph as if it were pure.  This is
             mainly intended for use with the ----ssttaattiicc flag and has no effect
             if ----sshhaarreedd is also specified.

     ----rreellooccaattee=_p_a_t_h
             Relocates a path using the pkgconf_path_relocate API.  This is
             mainly used by the testsuite to provide a guaranteed interface to
             the system's path relocation backend.

     ----sshhaarreedd
             Compute a simple dependency graph that is only suitable for
             shared linking.  This option overrides ----ssttaattiicc.

     ----sshhoorrtt--eerrrroorrss
             When printing error messages about modules that are not found or
